dsh-hot-reloader README · 它到底解决了什么问题：DSH **自带**热重载服务 [`@deepseek-ai/dsh-hmr`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@deepseek-ai/dsh-hmr)，但它对绝大多数插件都**不会生效**。原因很具体——它有两处硬编码把 `node_modules` 排除在外：

```js
// dsh-hmr/lib/index.js:201 —— loadDependencies()
if (job.url.startsWith("node:") || job.url.includes("/node_modules/")) return;

// dsh-hmr/lib/index.js:478 —— analyzeChanges()

而 DSH profile 安装的插件，**全部**位于：

```
~/.dsh/profiles/<profile>/node_modules/<包名>/
```

于是链路是这样断的：

dsh-hot-reloader README · 前置条件（本插件比别的插件更挑环境，务必先读）：```js
const hmr = ctx.get('hmr')
if (hmr && typeof hmr._resolve === 'function') { /* 用它的解析 */ }
// ...
if (hmr && typeof hmr.runExclusive === 'function') { await hmr.runExclusive(run) }

**两条路都有自实现兜底**：拿不到 `hmr` 时退回 `ctx.loader.internal.resolveSync`
与直接执行，插件照常工作。所以它是优化而非硬依赖。

不过它默认就是启用的，而且它的问题正是本插件存在的理由：

```yaml

dsh-hot-reloader README · 关于 Node 的 ESM 模块缓存：Node 24 的 ESM `LoadCache` 内部结构是这样的：

```js
class SafeMap extends Map {}
class LoadCache extends SafeMap {
  get(url, type = kImplicitTypeAttribute) { return super.get(url)?.[type] }
  set(url, type = kImplicitTypeAttribute, job) { /* 存成 url -> { [type]: job } */ }

也就是说：

- 它是**两层结构**：URL → `{ type: ModuleJob }`
- 它的 `delete()` **只把 type 槽置为 `undefined`，并不移除 key**

因此本插件（与宿主 `dsh-hmr` 的做法一致）用 `Map.prototype.delete.call(cache, url)` 绕过被重写的方法，确保条目被彻底移除；这样清理之后，模块会**真正重新执行**。

dsh-hot-reloader README · The problem it actually solves：DSH **ships** a hot-reload service, [`@deepseek-ai/dsh-hmr`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@deepseek-ai/dsh-hmr), but it will **not** fire for the vast majority of plugins. The reason is concrete — it hardcodes `node_modules` out of the picture in two places:

```js
// dsh-hmr/lib/index.js:201 —— loadDependencies()
if (job.url.startsWith("node:") || job.url.includes("/node_modules/")) return;

// dsh-hmr/lib/index.js:478 —— analyzeChanges()

And every plugin a DSH profile installs lives under:

dsh-hot-reloader README · Prerequisites (this plugin is pickier than most — please read)：This plugin **reuses** that service: module resolution goes through its `_resolve()`,
and replacement runs inside its `runExclusive()` transaction (so it never races the
built-in HMR).

```js
const hmr = ctx.get('hmr')
if (hmr && typeof hmr._resolve === 'function') { /* use its resolver */ }
// ...
if (hmr && typeof hmr.runExclusive === 'function') { await hmr.runExclusive(run) }

dsh-hot-reloader README · On Node's ESM module cache：This plugin's cache-clearing logic targets the internal structure of Node 24's `LoadCache`, whose real shape is:

```js
class SafeMap extends Map {}
class LoadCache extends SafeMap {
  get(url, type = kImplicitTypeAttribute) { return super.get(url)?.[type] }
  set(url, type = kImplicitTypeAttribute, job) { /* stores url -> { [type]: job } */ }

